Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:36:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10942/11362] Refine the cascade check: absent upstream is not
 a finding

Ran the proposed join by hand against the live 609 roadmap. It works and needs
one correction before anyone builds it.

Report-any-gate-whose-upstream-field-is-zero is right in principle, but a naive
implementation flags the wrong thing: seven of 609's twelve tasks gate on
upstreams that have not run yet, which is the normal state of a milestone in
progress and carries no signal. The rule must require that the upstream artifact
EXISTS and its field already fails the expected value.

Demonstrated rather than asserted. exp6942 was on disk with
v608_execution_contract_ready_score = 0 while ten tasks gated on it, so an
exists-and-fails rule fires there, and it stayed silent across all seven of 609's
gates. One true positive, seven true negatives.

Also records that 609 is currently clean by that rule, so no second cascade is
pending this hour.

